    "title": "Manhunt underway for suspect in fatal Antioch shooting - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Alex Baker ,\n4 hours ago\n( KRON ) — Police in Antioch have identified the suspect in a fatal shooting earlier this year. Zahvon Hopson is wanted in connection to the February 19 shooting that left a 20-year-old woman dead.\nHopson, according to the Antioch Police Department, should be considered armed and dangerous.\nOfficers initially responded on Feb. 19 at 7:17 p.m. to the 2200 block of Sycamore Drive on a report of a shooting. At the scene, officers located a woman suffering from at least one gunshot wound.\nScreaming naked man with shotgun arrested at Tesla service center in Berkeley She was pronounced dead at the scene.\nPolice say the suspect was identified through a combination of video surveillance, witness statements and forensic evidence. Police are advising anyone who sees Hopson not to confront him.\nZahvon Hopson mugshot (Antioch PD) Anyone who does see Hopson or has information on his whereabouts is asked to call 911 immediately. The Antioch Police Department is also urging Hopson to come forward and surrender peacefully.\nAntioch PD is also advising that anyone who assists Hopson in evading law enforcement or knowingly assists him in the future could be subject to arrest.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KRON4.\n7",
    "summary": "( KRON ) — Police in Antioch have identified the suspect in a fatal shooting earlier this year. Zahvon Hopson is wanted in connection to the February 19 shooting that left a 20-year-old woman dead. Screaming naked man with shotgun arrested at Tesla service center in Berkeley She was pronounced dead at the scene. Police say the suspect was identified through a combination of video surveillance, witness statements and forensic evidence. The Antioch Police Department is also urging Hopson to come forward and surrender peacefully.",
